# A fill on demand (the Sections screen's K3): left queues the drums' fill, right the comp's, the middle none; it plays
# on the last bar of the section playing (the drums' from beat 4, the comp's from beat 3), then K3 shows OFF again;
# queued once that bar's fill has begun, the next section's last bar. tests/scenarios/stutter.vnl's song: 56 bars at
# 81 BPM (2963 ms a bar, a 16th 185 ms, bar 1 from about 1.46 s): an 8-bar intro, four 8-bar grooves, two lead blocks.
listen
wait 1400
tap PLAY
wait 3000
tap SEL
wait 50
said SECTIONS
expect fill 0
# left: the drums', for the intro's last bar (bar 8, from 0: 7)
spin K3 -1
wait 50
said FILL DRUMS
expect fill 1
expect fill_at 7
expect fill_bar -1
expect stutter 0
shot fill-queued.png
# the intro's last bar, its beat 4 (24.4-25.2 s): the fill plays, K3 still shows it
wait 19850
expect bar 7
expect fill_bar 7
expect fill 1
# the next bar: played, OFF again, nothing waiting
wait 1500
expect bar 8
expect fill 0
expect fill_bar -1
expect fill_at -1
# right: the comp's, for the first groove's last bar (bar 16, from 0: 15); back to the middle, cancelled; right again
spin K3 1
wait 50
said FILL COMP
expect fill 2
expect fill_at 15
spin K3 -1
wait 50
said FILL OFF
expect fill 0
expect fill_at -1
spin K3 1
wait 50
said FILL COMP
expect fill 2
expect fill_at 15
# the first groove's last bar, past its beat 3 (47.6-48.9 s): the comp's fill plays
wait 21500
expect bar 15
expect fill_bar 15
expect fill 2
shot fill-playing.png
# past that bar's beat 4 (its 14th 16th, about 48.4 s), turned left past the middle (through OFF: the rest of the comp's
# cancelled), the drums': theirs has begun there, so they wait for the next section's last bar (bar 24, from 0: 23),
# shown meanwhile
wait 650
turn K3 -2 20
wait 50
said FILL DRUMS
expect bar 15
expect fill 1
expect fill_at 23
expect fill_bar -1
wait 1000
expect bar 16
expect fill 1
# bar 24's beat 4 (71.8-72.6 s)
wait 22560
expect bar 23
expect fill_bar 23
expect fill 1
wait 1500
expect bar 24
expect fill 0
